Syntax: distill <item>

Distill destroys a piece of jewelry and draws what it carried into essence.

Only jewelry.  A shaman's bangle is how anything else becomes distillable,
which is why the two skills stand together.

Every stat on the piece deposits, not one chosen from among them: a ring of
strength and dexterity yields both.  How much depends on the size of the
stat and on how well you know the work, and it is never nothing.

What you deposit goes into an essence of that stat you already carry, if you
have one, rather than making a second.  That is what lets essence grow at
all -- charges scattered across duplicates never reach anything.

Armor is not among the stats an essence can hold.  Armor belongs to the
body, and to the smiths.

See also: INFUSE, BANGLE, ESSENCE
